      "speaker": "mother",
      "text": "You have to put more of the roasted garlic in your potatoes, Jeffrey. You always were a bit of a picky eater."
    },
    {
      "speaker": "Jeffrey",
      "text": "I'm not picky, Mom. I just appreciate the balance. And honestly, this is much better than the takeout we had last week."
    },
    {
      "speaker": "mother",
      "text": "It is nice to sit down properly. The house feels full when we're both here."
    },
    {
      "speaker": "Jeffrey",
      "text": "It does. You know, I was sitting on the patio earlier and I caught a whiff of something—a certain kind of dampness in the air—and it took me straight back to the Bay Area."
    },
    {
      "speaker": "mother",
      "text": "The fog? Or the salt?"
    },
    {
      "speaker": "Jeffrey",
      "text": "It was definitely the fog. That heavy, grey mist that would roll over the hills so quickly it felt like the world was just shrinking around our backyard."
    },
    {
      "speaker": "mother",
      "text": "Oh, I remember those mornings! You used to complain that it ruined your hair, but I loved it. I remember standing by the window with my coffee, watching the grass turn that specific shade of deep emerald. It felt like we were living inside a painting."
    },
    {
      "speaker": "Jeffrey",
      "text": "I don't think I ever complained that much. I just remember how quiet everything got. It was like the world held its breath."
    },
    {
      "speaker": "mother",
      "text": "It did. It was a very different kind of quiet than we have here now. But it was a good life we had there, too."
    },
    {
      "speaker": "Jeffrey",
      "text": "It was. And I’m glad we have these memories. Even when I'm here in LA, working and seeing my girlfriend, I still find myself thinking about those foggy mornings."
    },
    {
      "speaker": "mother",
      "text": "She's a lucky girl to have you, and you're lucky to have her. But I'm glad she's not at the table tonight. It's nice to just have our time."
    },
    {
      "speaker": "Jeffrey",
      "text": "It is. It's funny, isn't it? We've traveled so far from those hills. From that house to this house."
    },
    {
      "speaker": "mother",
      "text": "We have. But the table is still the same, isn't it? It's still about the food, and the company, and the stories."
    },
    {
      "speaker": "Jeffrey",
      "text": "Exactly. I really appreciate this, Mom. Just sitting here with you."
    },
    {
      "speaker": "mother",
      "text": "I appreciate it too, honey. Pass me that pitcher of water, would you? This is a very good dinner."
    },
    {
      "speaker": "Jeffrey",
      "text": "It really is."
    }
  ]
}

